.TH CHACHATEST 1
.SH NAME
chachatest \- test keyring's raw ChaCha20 stream and one-shot Poly1305
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B chachatest
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Chachatest
checks the three keyring primitives the
.B chacha20-poly1305@openssh.com
construction of
.IR ssh (1)
needs beyond the RFC 8439 AEAD wrapper that
.IR ccpolytest (1)
already covers:
.B chacha_setblock
(seek the ChaCha20 block counter),
.B chacha_encrypt
(raw stream, no Poly1305 tag), and
.B poly1305
(a one-shot tag under a caller-supplied one-time key). The vectors
are RFC 8439's own published examples \(em the ChaCha20 encryption
example of \(sc2.4.2 and the Poly1305 example of \(sc2.5.2 \(em not a
reimplementation:
.IP \(bu
Poly1305 over the standard's 34-byte message under its key must
equal the standard's tag;
.IP \(bu
ChaCha20 of the standard's plaintext, with the block counter set to
1 as the example specifies, must equal the standard's ciphertext;
.IP \(bu
the same encryption with the block counter left at 0 must
.I not
match \(em an automated negative control proving
.B chacha_setblock
is actually consulted (a wrong keystream is a safe computation, so
this one can be automated, unlike a memory-hazard control).
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/cmd/chachatest.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR ccpolytest (1),
.IR keyring (2)
.SH BUGS
Coverage is the two fixed RFC vectors plus the block-counter control.
Poly1305 is exercised one-shot only; the streaming state that
.IR ccpolytest (1)
covers is not re-tested here.
